			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 14 submodules with PascalCase modularization and RPC expansion\n\nSynchronize 14 Element submodules to align the codebase with the strict PascalCase naming convention and the new distributed 'file-per-struct' architecture.\n\nMountain undergoes a massive structural refactor: decomposing monolithic modules (Vine, ApplicationState, RPC handlers) into dedicated submodules (e.g., `Vine::Client::ConnectToSideCar::Fn`, `ApplicationState::State::ApplicationState::State`), enforcing explicit `::Fn`/`::Struct` resolution for Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro. This includes implementing the full `Vine` gRPC contract for `Cocoon` (file system, SCM, Debug, Task, Authentication, Test providers) and adding robust state recovery primitives (`MementoLoader`, `RecoverStateWithBackoff`) to prevent boot crashes from corrupted state. Mountain also introduces foundational infrastructure: cross-platform process introspection, PostHog telemetry plugin, shell environment injection for GUI launches, and updated Tauri entitlements to disable sandboxing for extension compatibility.\n\nOther submodules (Air, Common, Echo, Grove, Mist, Rest, SideCar) update their `Documentation/Rust` references to the latest upstream standards. Sky bumps `zod` and `@xterm/xterm` dependencies, while Cocoon, Output, Wind, and Worker sync to the latest commits to maintain consistency across the IPC boundary.\n\nThese changes establish a consistent, testable namespace hierarchy, resolve symbol resolution issues during IPC generation, and ensure the editor can launch reliably from both CLI and GUI contexts with full extension host capabilities.",
			"SHA": "90ecc25ecc3e48eed4ae2546ee97d17d04e8f5e7"
		}
